Step-by-Step: Auto Debug CMake Projects in VSCodium
1. Install the CMake Tools Extension

You've likely done this, but just in case:

codium --install-extension ms-vscode.cmake-tools

2. Open a CMake Project in VSCodium

Make sure your project has a CMakeLists.txt at the root.

Example structure:

my-project/
├── CMakeLists.txt
├── src/
│   └── main.cpp

3. Configure and Build Automatically

Once the project is opened:

    Press Ctrl+Shift+P, then run:

CMake: Configure

Then run:

    CMake: Build

CMake Tools will:

    Generate the build/ directory

    Detect targets

    Build the binaries

4. Automatically Debug Any Target

You can now debug any target in one click:

    Press Ctrl+Shift+P → select:

	CMake: Debug Target

	Choose your target (like main or my_app)

	The debugger (GDB) will launch automatically, even without launch.json.

